# Normalise line endings. Without this, a contributor on Windows can commit
# CRLF into a shell script and it will stop running on Linux with an error
# message that mentions nothing about line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# GitHub guesses a repository's language by counting code and ignoring prose,
# which made this book show up as 47% C and 20% Python. The book is 315 KB of
# writing and 70 KB of code. Mark the supporting code as documentation so the
# language bar reflects what this actually is.
tools/*        linguist-documentation
*/code/**      linguist-documentation
*/tests/**     linguist-documentation
*.md           linguist-detectable
